      "writtenOn": "2025-09-17T15:05:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wondering if we really need mitigate_bhi(), since IIUC `boot_cpu_has(X86_BUG_BHI) \u0026\u0026 !boot_cpu_has(X86_BUG_SPECTRE_V2)` is not supposed to happen, so mitigate_spectre_v2() should always take care of enabling BHI mitigation if needed?\n\nAlthough it may cause the below \"Cannot mitigate CPU bug\" being erroneously printed (not in this case, since X86_BUG_SPECTRE_V1 \u003c X86_BUG_BHI, but maybe in a more general case). But we may remove this print, as I suggested below?\n\nEDIT: please feel free to ignore this, I\u0027ve just realized that mitigate_spectre_v2() may not succeed and then mitigate_bhi() may succeed (that is actually the case on ADL, for instance), i.e. it is actually useful if we cannot mitigate Spectre V2 as a whole but at least can mitigate just BHI.",
      "revId": "31fba6288ad05b18388ed84f72966f24ae37fd42",
